# Corpse family binding disposition

Ordinary character corpse creation calls the explicit family binding helper
with an empty list, accompanied by a comment saying there is no authoritative
kinship relation. Current estate succession does consult explicit child
kinship and marriage records. The helper accepts at most eight supplied
settlement-resident NPCs in the corpse settlement; it does not itself derive
kin from the deceased. Demo setup explicitly supplies a resident.

Corpse-family bindings affect family permission classification and social
consequences for unauthorized handling, burning and bypassing family. Whether
ordinary character relatives should populate those bindings, and which
relatives meet residence and timing rules, is a product-policy question; the
source does not establish a reachable omitted qualifying relative. Historical
full-body corpse source and continuity match the selected revision exactly.
After the audit gate decide and validate the supported relationship policy.
